# Xcode
#^=The specification is internally consistent as a governance and ingestion model. The leading symbolic sequence:

=%#=A+.7=
LoGoS.olos.6185:85ad(MS::CD)

should be treated as project-defined symbolic identifiers unless a formal encoding is specified. Without a documented grammar or decoder, no semantic interpretation should be asserted beyond recording them as observed tokens.

A refined version that incorporates those identifiers while preserving the governance principles is:

RESOLVE_RAW_INPUT_BINARY
Identifier:
    LoGoS.olos.6185:85ad(MS::CD)
Observed Symbolic Sequence:
    =%#=A+.7=
Classification:
    PROJECT_DEFINED
    STATUS: OBSERVED
    SEMANTICS: NOT_ESTABLISHED
Purpose:
    Preserve the original binary input exactly as acquired while enabling
    deterministic, governed selection and subsequent interpretation.
Canonical Pipeline
Raw Input
    │
    ▼
Binary Acquisition
    │
    ▼
Binary Set (B)
    │
    ▼
Governed Mask (M)
    │
    ▼
Selection (S = B ∧ M)
    │
    ▼
Decode
    │
    ▼
Tokenization
    │
    ▼
Canonical Representation
    │
    ▼
Schema Validation
    │
    ▼
Evidence Commitment
    │
    ▼
Registry Reference
Mathematical Definition
B = { b_i | b_i ∈ {0,1} }
M = { m_i | m_i ∈ {0,1} }
S = B ∧ M
Selection Function
Select(Graph, Rules, Context)
    ↓
Selected Binary
    ↓
Decoded Artifact
    ↓
Governed Object
Governance Invariants
• Raw binary is immutable.
• Canonical identities are stable.
• Masks are governed and versioned.
• Selection is deterministic for governed inputs.
• Decoding is reproducible for a given decoder version.
• Evidence accumulates monotonically.
• Every generated artifact retains complete provenance.
• Non-governed inputs are rejected or quarantined prior to selection.
• Commitment is a governed write and is separate from selection.
