Evidence Boundary
Binary acquisition, masking, decoding, and validation establish governed
artifacts above the Evidence Boundary.
Claims regarding formal verification or operational execution require new,
independently reviewable evidence below the Evidence Boundary.
Status
Observed binary source: ESTABLISHED
Governed selection model: ESTABLISHED
Formal semantics of the symbolic sequence: NOT_ESTABLISHED

This preserves an important distinction: the symbolic strings (=%#=A+.7= and LoGoS.olos.6185:85ad(MS::CD)) are valid as identifiers or observed inputs within your governance framework, but their meaning should remain explicitly project-defined and not established until a formal grammar, encoding specification, or decoding evidence is added to the repository. This is consistent with the Resolve Kernel’s principle of separating observation, governed representation, and verified interpretation.
